                <pb facs="0101" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 28.</note>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Davis to Mr. E. B. Washburne.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 6, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>It appearing by your last dispatch that new government is fully installed and
                    Paris remains tranquil, you will recognize.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>DAVIS, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
